ome. Remaining performance obligations were $638 billion, and unconditional purchase commitments for cloud infrastructure assets were $19 billion."}],"prose":{"overview":"ORACLE CORP (ORCL) reported trailing-year revenue of $67.4 billion and expenses of $47.6 billion. The ledger shows $37.4 billion in total committed money, including debt, leases, and purchases. It also shows $638.0 billion in backlog and $15.4 billion in deferred revenue.","debt":"Reported debt is $7.2 billion. Total committed money is $37.4 billion, including $7.2 billion of debt, $30.2 billion of leases, and $0 million of purchases. Debt therefore represents only part of the commitments shown in the filings.","wall":"The filings show $110.7 billion of obligations due in the next five years. They show $0 million due in the following five to ten years and $0 million beyond ten years. The ledger lists $0 million of future revenue for the next five years, while backlog is $638.0 billion.","flags_note":"The filings report additional operating lease commitments that were not recorded on the balance sheets, including $248 billion at November 30, 2025. They also report guarantees of lessor borrowings associated with leases, increasing from $2.2 billion to $3.3 billion. Other disclosures changed across filings, including the recognition horizon and allocation of remaining performance obligations."}}